{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/708317-does-anyone-know-the-origin-on-this-myth","id":708317,"title":"Does anyone know the origin on this myth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-19T00:38:57-07:00","id":708317,"title":"Does anyone know the origin on this myth","content":"I read an unsourced statement on wikipedia that V\u00e9 (sometimes Lodurr), brother of Odin, was banished to the &quot;underworld&quot; (NIfleheim I assume?) for attempting to usurp the Allfather. I have never heard this before, and I'm wondering if its total b.s. or if anyone knows a source on this story?<br /> <br /> There's also a claim that V\u00e9 might be Baldr's true father?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T07:53:16-07:00","id":708739,"title":"","content":"I'm not exactly an expert on the matter, but the books I've read pretty much involve Vili and V\u00e9 fading into the background after the three of them brought life to the first mortals. Certainly I've never read about any of them taking the fore, let alone in a coup attempt.<br /> <br /> Loki does accuse Frigg of bedding Odin's brothers, so it's possibly not inconceivable that one of them could have sired Baldr if he were telling the truth but I don't believe I've ever come across any writings that say it. Loki didn't accuse Baldr of being V\u00e9 or Vili's child in Lokasenna. I suppose you could infer it if you wanted to, but that's not the same as fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T01:56:12-07:00","id":712084,"title":"","content":"What you are looking for is Snorri Sturlusons Ynglinga Saga. More specifically Chapter Three. In a nutshell, Odin was away from Asgard for so long that he was thought dead and both Villi and Ve took Frigg as their mistress for a short amount of time, as detailed by Loki. As to the claim of Ve being Baldr's true father, nothing comes up from memory right now, but I'll investigate further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8325,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","user":"Asmael","date":". 10-21-2015, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T13:00:23-07:00","id":712923,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Anything about Ve being banished to the underworld (Niflheim? I'd assume?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:12:20-07:00","id":713076,"title":"","content":"Well, going over my resources (The Internet, books from the time when I majored in German studies and notes for my own campaign) the only relevant stuff I could dig out is this: <br /> <br /> Vili and V\u00e9 are creator deities alongside Odin, but have little to no relevance outside of a context with or at least in some proximity to him. I.E. to speak of Vili and V\u00e9 is to speak of Odin too, at least indirectly. Seems like this comes from the time back when Odin was called &quot;Wodanaz&quot; (or at least something similar) which translates roughly to &quot;Lord of Inspiration&quot;, &quot;Seer&quot;, &quot;Bard&quot; or &quot;(to) Inspire&quot; while Vili means something along the lines of &quot;Spirit&quot; and V\u00e9 roughly translates to &quot;Sanctum&quot;. So a theory would be that they are aspects of the same god or a later introduction to the Norse Canon by Christian missionaries. But thats beside the point. <br /> <br /> While this of course makes for some interesting ideas as to what that war really was, the only thing I could find are some German texts which, in a nutshell, say this: Odin left Asgard in some texts prior to Sturluson, but apparently he didn't do so on his own free will as Sturloson wrote it. It's more likely that he practised the art of Seidr (fate-weaving magic) which was forbidden to men (meaning only women were allowed to use it) and got thrown out of Asgard for it. There are dozen myths like this in other cultures, of course, so the rough scheme fits the bill. There might very well be a source older than Sturlosons translations (which had been made when the religion of the Aesir was already at the verge of becoming extinct) which states the circumstances you've mentioned, but I'm not sure if they'll be easy to find outside an academic context. If someone manages to either way, feel free to correct me there. <br /> <br /> Sorry I couldn't be of more help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T19:50:26-07:00","id":713536,"title":"","content":"I can help a bit on this to shed some light on it, though I can't say I'm familiar with V\u00e9 being &quot;banished&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> while Vili means something along the lines of &quot;Spirit&quot; and V\u00e9 roughly translates to &quot;Sanctum&quot;. So a theory would be that they are aspects of the same god or a later introduction to the Norse Canon by Christian missionaries. </div> </div> </div>When humans were first created, Hoenir (Vili) Gave Hugr to man, Odin gave them Hamingja and L\u00f3\u00f0ur gave them Hamr. They are the same as Bor's sons, Vili, V\u00e9 and Odin, the names only make sense when you bring them back to their old Germanic forms, where they are alliterative. They are roughly analogous to the Hindu Brahma, Shiva and Vishnu and the other indo-european &quot;three Brothers&quot;. Most certainly not a christian invention, they predate Christianity as a religion by a landslide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Odin left Asgard in some texts prior to Sturluson, but apparently he didn't do so on his own free will as Sturloson wrote it. It's more likely that he practiced the art of Seidr (fate-weaving magic) which was forbidden to men (meaning only women were allowed to use it) and got thrown out of Asgard for it. </div> </div> </div>When Baldr was slain by Loki Odin used his magic to learn the best way to gain revenge on the matter, and learned that he should impregnate the Giantess Rindr, for she would give birth to Vali who would avenge his brother (And himself at Ragnarok). The only problem was that Rindr wanted nothing to do with Odin and rebuffed his advances. Not the one to be turned down, he proceeded to drug her, tie her to a bed and rape her. After Vali was born and avenged his brother, Odin was banished from Asgard for 10 years for the crime, where he wandered the world until his return.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I read an unsourced statement on wikipedia that V\u00e9 (sometimes Lodurr), brother of Odin, was banished to the &quot;underworld&quot; (NIfleheim I assume?) for attempting to usurp the Allfather. I have never heard this before, and I'm wondering if its total b.s. or if anyone knows a source on this story? </div> </div> </div>As mentioned, there is a story that during one of Odin's longer travels the court of Asgard thought him lost or slain, and his brothers took up the kingship, but could not decide amongst themselves who should reign. They both took Frigg to wife and decided to rule together (There is a Norse tradition of a Land king and a Sea King, this might be the Ur-Example actually). When Odin returned he was of course wroth to find his wife with his brothers and thought the worst. Loki didn't help matters by claiming that his brothers sought to depose him and Frigg had whored herself to them to keep her position as queen. Eventually Odin discovered the truth of the matter, but he almost had all three of them executed.<br /> <br /> My guess is that someone misread something as &quot;Banished to the underworld&quot; is quite clearly a euphemism for Died, when all three are supposed to have been saved by the skin if their teeth from the misunderstanding. Alternatively, perhaps there was an alternate version in which one of the brothers WAS executed before the truth was found out, but i would honestly expect them to all have faced the same execution, and that obviously isn't the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T23:03:17-07:00","id":713771,"title":"","content":"So for a story set after the death of Baldur, with Odin reigning in Asgard, Ve/Lodurr would in all liklihood be a minor member of his court - perhaps politically forsaken in favor of more famous deities specifically because of his past pseudo-usurpation, right?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Vili/Hoenir is off with the Vanir tribes, helplessly Mimir-less. A nominal hostage (just as Njord and his kids are in Asgard), but one Odin cares very little about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Any take on the two Valis? There's Odin's son born specifically to avenge Baldr. But there's also a son of Loki who is transformed into a wolf to kill his brother Narfi after the same events, so Narfi's entrails can be used to bind Loki. The revenge for Baldur's death parallel seems pretty major to just be two different Aesir with the same name. Perhaps conceptually the same god, but with different origin myths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-22-2015, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T08:49:55-07:00","id":714643,"title":"","content":"&quot;in<span style=\"color:#000000\"> Ursula Dronke's </span>translation in her edition of the poem, &quot;Then did V\u00e1li | slaughter bonds twist&quot;.This presumably refers to Vali, son of Odin, who was begotten to avenge Baldr's death, and thus it is not unlikely that he bound Loki; but the <i>Hauksb\u00f3k</i> stanza interrupts the flow of &quot;V\u00f6lusp\u00e1&quot; at this point and presumably draws on a variant oral tradition. It is likely that this was Snorri's source and that he interpreted the manuscript text <i>V\u00e1la v\u00edgb\u01ebnd</i> as &quot;bonds from V\u00e1li's act of slaughter&quot;, thus inventing a second V\u00e1li&quot;<br /> <br /> I think thats a good answer for the issue, that there isin't two Vali's, Snorri just misinterpreted a line.<br /> <br /> Odin would care very much for his brother, not only would he have the familiar family bond that everyone knows, but he would be obligated to protect and support him as a duty. As for Ve's position in the &quot;Court&quot; of Asgard, its a bit of a non issue as Traditional Germanic kingship doesn't work in the same way as a medieval christian court would. There are roughly two positions. King (First among equals) and Nobles (Everyone else). I guess there could also be non noble classes, but they are likely to be pretty irrelevant in a story, probably Alfar or Dwarves in the position of servants or pages, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}